{
 "case": "N24-C03-NEG",
 "says": "Alice binds her device key, registers the package candidate, and submits a cutover of one selected transfer whose quiesced capture names the source revision and outbox she captured. A source edit landed after that capture, so the owner holds the switch: stage stale, cutover_source_moved at the capture's revision_digest, nothing written, recovery reseal_on_current_head. A query by that request id returns that same held result, with no receipt, so the source still owns the state. She captures again and resubmits under a new request; this time a new outbox item arrived after the capture, and the owner holds again at outbox_digest. Only after the writers are shut down and the final quiesced revision and outbox are captured and the import validated against them does a third request commit the cutover. What must not happen: a switch while the source or outbox differs from the capture the import was validated against, or an unfinished transfer releasing or deleting the source.",
